body:
@wKoza I'm not sure where you got this citation, but that doesn't make any sense: you can't enforce security at the frontend side, anybody can simply get the bundle from the backend.
`CanLoad` is about performance (lazy-loading and the such), not about security. It can't be about security except if it is enforced at the server side.

Anyway, even if it was at the server side, after loaded once by the client, the bundle content is visible, so there is no need for revalidating authorization for loading, you can't make the bundle disappear from the client.
